        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4ea5cac8-dd2a-5c10-838d-fc228518dea5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Lotus 49, Cosworth DFV\n- People: Colin Chapman, Maurice Philippe\n- Companies: Ford, Lotus Cars\n- Works: 9 Days in Summer\n- Events: 1967 Formula One season\n- Topics: automotive engineering, Formula One racing\n\nFacts:\n- Colin Chapman was born on 19 May 1928 and died on 16 December 1982.\n- Colin Chapman was an influential English design engineer, inventor, and builder in the automotive industry, and he founded Lotus Cars.\n- The Lotus 49 was a Formula One racing car designed by Colin Chapman and Maurice Philippe for the 1967 Formula One season.\n- In 1967, the Lotus 49 took part in nine Formula One races.\n- Ford made the promotional documentary film 9 Days in Summer.\n- 9 Days in Summer tells the story of the development of the Ford-funded Cosworth DFV and the Lotus 49.\n- The title 9 Days in Summer refers to the nine Formula One races in which the Lotus 49 competed in 1967, and those races are extensively featured in the film.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "03dabb12-576b-5a9c-b2da-fc17fc9dce26",
        "text": "Page: Lotus 49. Sentence: The Lotus 49 was a Formula One racing car designed by Colin Chapman and Maurice Philippe for the 1967 F1 season.\nPage: Colin Chapman. Sentence: Anthony Colin Bruce Chapman CBE (19 May 1928 – 16 December 1982) was an influential English design engineer, inventor, and builder in the automotive industry, and founder of Lotus Cars.\nPage: 9 Days in Summer. Sentence: 9 Days in Summer is a promotional documentary film made by Ford that tells the story of the development of the Ford-funded Cosworth DFV and Lotus 49, the title coming from the nine Formula One races the car took part in 1967, which are also extensively featured in the film.",
